2026-09-22 23:46:00,563 | INFO | [buffett] [agents] name=researcher mode=backtesting model=gemini-3.5-flash-lite cache_hit=False tokens_in=252948 tokens_out=1288 tokens_cached_in=169984 tokens_uncached_in=82964 tokens_thinking=0 tokens_total=254236 latency_ms=16844 first_event_latency_ms=2291 tool_calls=20 observability_warnings=0 summary="I have reviewed the SEC filings and fundamental facts for the requested universe (`AAPL`, `KO`, `AXP`, `JPM`) point-in-time as of January 5, 2026, and ranked the businesses by economic moat, financial strength, and free cash flow generation:  1. **AAPL (Apple Inc.)**    - **Rank:** 1    - **Rationale:** Exceptional economic moat built on unmatched brand loyalty, ecosystem lock-in, and pricing power. Generated $111.5B in operating cash flow and ~$98.8B in free cash flow in FY2025, alongside massive capital return via share repurchases ($90.7B) and dividends ($15.4B). High return on equity and pristine operational execution.  2. **JPM (JPMorgan Chase & Co.)**    - **Rank:** 2    - **Rationale:** Premier global financial institution possessing a fortress balance sheet ($360.2B in stockholders' equity, robust capital ratios) and exceptional underwriting and management. Demonstrated extraordinary earnings power with over $44B in net income in the first nine months of 2025.  3. **AXP (American Express Company)**    - **Rank:** 3    - **Rationale:** High-quality closed-loop payments network targeting affluent cardmembers who exhibit lower credit sensitivity during economic cycles. Generates strong cash flows ($13.7B FCF over the trailing 9-month annualized period) and maintains high returns on equity.  4. **KO (The Coca-Cola Company)**    - **Rank:** 4    - **Rationale:** Classic consumer staple with an unmatched global distribution network and brand moat. Highly stable and predictable cash flows, though top-line and earnings growth rates are more modest compared to technology and premier financial institutions.  RESULT: Read public filings and fundamentals for AAPL, KO, AXP, and JPM, evaluated their financial statements and balance sheets, and ranked their business quality in agent memory." trace=/Users/robertgrzesik/Library/Caches/lumibot/1.0/agent_runtime/traces/researcher/c04cd79a0ff14274c33c9227b9728010207a9ad24ba6ac65f647c9be07a26146-20260923034600534897.json
