2026-09-22 23:47:14,614 | INFO | [buffett] [agents] name=interpreter mode=backtesting model=gemini-3.5-flash-lite cache_hit=False tokens_in=22322 tokens_out=578 tokens_cached_in=16189 tokens_uncached_in=6133 tokens_thinking=0 tokens_total=22900 latency_ms=2450 first_event_latency_ms=2450 tool_calls=0 observability_warnings=1 summary="Based on the comprehensive fundamental analysis, point-in-time SEC filings review, and evaluation of economic moats, cash generation, balance sheet strength, and margins of safety as of January 6, 2026, here is the evaluation and assigned portfolio weightings for the research universe (`AAPL`, `JPM`, `AXP`, `KO`):  ### Evaluation & Margin of Safety Analysis  1. **Apple Inc. (AAPL)** — **Rank 1 | Assigned Weight: 40%**    - **Quality & Price Assessment:** Unrivaled consumer ecosystem lock-in, pristine operational execution, massive cash generation ($111.5B operating cash flow and ~$98.8B FCF in FY2025), and massive capital return ($90.7B in buybacks and $15.4B in dividends). It clears the margin of safety hurdle as our highest-conviction compounder. Currently held in the portfolio (146 shares).  2. **JPMorgan Chase & Co. (JPM)** — **Rank 2 | Assigned Weight: 30%**    - **Quality & Price Assessment:** Premier global financial institution with a fortress balance sheet ($360.2B in stockholders' equity) and elite underwriting discipline. Over $44B in net income in the first nine months of 2025 demonstrates unmatched earnings power. Clearly clears the margin of safety hurdle. Currently held in the portfolio (93 shares).  3. **American Express Company (AXP)** — **Rank 3 | Assigned Weight: 20%**    - **Quality & Price Assessment:** Superior closed-loop payments network targeting affluent, lower-credit-sensitivity cardmembers with strong high-return-on-equity compounding and strong FCF generation (~$13.7B annualized). Its resilience during economic shocks justifies a solid 20% allocation. Currently held in the portfolio (54 shares).  4. **The Coca-Cola Company (KO)** — **Rank 4 | Assigned Weight: 0%**    - **Quality & Price Assessment:** While KO possesses an unmatched global distribution network and defensive moat, its top-line organic growth is modest, and at current market pricing, it does not offer a sufficiently compelling margin of safety compared to our top three compounders (`AAPL`, `JPM`, `AXP`). Therefore, no weight or capital is assigned to KO.  ---  RESULT: Evaluated quality and price for AAPL, JPM, AXP, and KO, determined that AAPL (40%), JPM (30%), and AXP (20%) clear the margin of safety (while KO at 0% does not), and assigned portfolio weights without executing new orders." trace=/Users/robertgrzesik/Library/Caches/lumibot/1.0/agent_runtime/traces/interpreter/f56d925a6e2124b969bb5fd3df41916a5be9fa7b67bf1616a582cb91753a2bf4-20260923034714589192.json
